.TH GLAZE-SHELL 1 "2026-11-10" "Glaze 0.1.0" "Glaze User Commands"
.SH NAME
glaze-shell \- the Glaze GTK4 panel, launcher, clock and taskbar
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glaze-shell
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B glaze-shell
is the visible Glaze shell: a bottom panel anchored with
.BR gtk4-layer-shell ,
a distinct Glaze (start) button, a pinned-application area, running-window task
buttons, a status/tray area and a clock, plus the launcher popover. It is
written with GTK4 and styled with CSS generated from Glaze's design tokens; it is
not a web or Electron surface.
.PP
.B IMPLEMENTATION STATUS:
the shell source tree
.RB ( apps/glaze-shell )
is not present in this repository snapshot, and no
.B glaze-shell
executable has been built. The crate tree
.B glaze-shell-core
that will hold the GTK-free shell logic (panel ordering, the launcher state
machine, clock formatting and task grouping) currently defines only its crate
root; its modules are being added by the shell workstream. The
.B glaze-session
component graph already lists
.B glaze-shell
as a component, so the session will start it once it exists.
.PP
The interaction model this command will implement is documented for users in
.BR docs/user-guide.md :
the Glaze button opens the launcher; typing filters real installed
applications; the up and down arrow keys move the selection; Enter launches the
selected application; Escape closes the launcher; clicking outside the launcher
dismisses it and returns keyboard focus. Glaze Clay is the default theme and Glaze
Classic is the heritage alternative, each in light and dark. The theme and
behaviour are driven by
.BR ~/.config/glaze/config.toml .
.SH OPTIONS
None documented. Option and window-manager flag handling will be added together
with the shell binary; this page will be updated to match the code, not the
other way round.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
The shell renders as a Wayland layer-shell client and requires a running
compositor.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Location of
.BR glaze/config.toml .
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Location of the
.B glaze-service
control socket it talks to.
.TP
.B XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP
Set to
.B Glaze
by
.BR glaze-session (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Clean shutdown. Not reachable until the binary exists.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glaze (1),
.BR glaze-session (1),
.BR glaze-settings (1),
.BR glaze-service (1),
.BR glaze-compositor (1)
